
EXERCISE 6: Basic Linux Commands
Date: 10. Aug. 2026
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Aim: To study and practice basic Linux commands required for ethical hacking.
Tools Required: Kali Linux terminal.
Theory:
Linux commands are essential for navigating the file system, managing files, and running
tools. Ethical hackers must be comfortable with the command line.
Procedure:
# Navigation
pwd # Print working directory
ls # List files
ls -la # List all files with details
cd /etc # Change directory
cd .. # Go back one level
# File Management
mkdir lab # Create directory
touch test.txt # Create empty file
cp test.txt copy.txt # Copy file
mv copy.txt /tmp/ # Move file
rm test.txt # Remove file
cat /etc/passwd # View file contents
nano test.txt # Edit file
# Permissions
chmod 755 test.txt # Change permissions
chown kali test.txt # Change owner
# System Information
whoami # Current user
id # User ID and groups
uname -a # System information
hostname # System name
ip a # IP address
ifconfig # Network interfaces
